  "article_notes": "Two groups of 4 Labrador dogs with B. canis (smear) of low vs high parasite intensity, plus 6 healthy controls (Zoolux clinic, Kyiv, and university laboratory). All significance tests are vs controls only; the high- vs low-intensity values are therefore extracted as descriptive_only (mean ± m). Haemoglobinuria (brown urine) was noted in 3 high-intensity dogs, with no count reported for the low group, so not extracted. Very small groups (n=4). Bilirubin has two rows (total and direct).",
